      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1334",
      "html": "<p>Lithoxus is a genus of small, rheophilic loricariids that are externally characterized by a strongly dorsoventrally depressed body, a large round oral disk, and small tooth cups with few teeth.</p><p>Etymology: Greek, lithos = stone + Greek, oxys = sharp.</p>"
